# {{ customer }} — {{ solution }} Technologies

## Purpose

Define the technology products, managed services, and technical platforms that materially realize or constrain the architecture.

## Boundary Rules

Include identifiable storage engines, integration platforms, event services, analytical platforms, application platforms, search services, and material storage or exchange patterns. Keep sources and data products in their own inventories even when implemented using named technology.

## Technology Classification

| Classification | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Data storage platform | Stores analytical, operational, or exchange data. |
| Data integration platform | Acquires, transforms, orchestrates, or delivers data. |
| Event integration services | Carries and processes event-driven data. |
| Analytical consumption platform | Enables interactive consumption of governed information. |
| Operational application platform | Hosts a business process integrated with the solution. |
| Search and indexing platform | Indexes data for search and discovery. |
| Enterprise application platform | Provides an enterprise capability and integration boundary. |

